['The purpose of the tutorial is to facilitate in-depth discussions on a more specific issue related to our lectures.', '', 'Discussions play an important role in learning as it helps to deepen your understanding and develop your own ideas.', '', 'Besides this, if you can explain something to others clearly, then you really understand it.', '', 'If you can’t, you don’t!', '', ' So, the discussion is also an effective way for you to examine how much you have understood in class.', '', 'The harvest of our tutorials largely depends on your active participation and contribution.', '', 'Thus, be proactive and talkative!', 'Setting', 'There are altogether 8 tutorial sessions if the briefing session isn’t included. ', ' ', '', 'You are supposed to read those articles before attending the tutorials.', 'Tutorial readings have been uploaded to Moodle.', 'Time Limit: Each presentation should not exceed 15 minutes so that a sufficient amount of time is left for discussion.', 'It’s great if you can make a presentation outline to your classmates. Yet, it’s optional.', '', 'Assessment', 'The tutorial will constitute 30% of your total grade.', 'Your tutorial mark depends on three parts: 10% on group presentation, 10% on discussion and 10% on Debate.', 'As for the presentation, tutor will evaluate students’ performance on these perspectives:', 'Do the presenters understand the article properly and thoroughly?', 'Can they re-construct the arguments hidden and express them with their own words precisely?', 'Can they have a logical, critical reflection on the article?', 'Can they raise some controversial but important questions to kick off the discussion?', 'As for the discussion, tutor will assess students’ performance by following criteria:', 'Do they read the articles carefully?', 'Do they take the initiative to express their opinions?', 'Do they try to respond to questions raised by the presenters and have constructive interaction with fellow classmates?', 'Can they articulate their ideas clearly and fluently?', 'Regarding the debate, ', 'Can they provide valid and persuasive arguments to support their stance?', 'Can they refute opponents’ arguments with strong reasons/evidence?', 'Those who come late more than 15 minutes may risk a mark penalty.']
['The purpose of the tutorial is to facilitate in-depth discussions on a more specific issue related to our lectures. ', '', 'Discussions play an important role in learning as it helps to deepen your understanding and develop your own ideas. ', '', 'Besides this, if you can explain something to others clearly, then you really understand it. ', '', 'If you can’t, you don’t! ', '', 'So, the discussion is also an effective way for you to examine how much you have understood in class. ', '', 'The harvest of our tutorials largely depends on your active participation and contribution. ', '', 'Thus, be proactive and talkative!', '', 'Setting', 'There are altogether 8 tutorial sessions if the briefing session isn’t included. ', ' ', '', 'You are supposed to read those articles before attending the tutorials.', 'Tutorial readings have been uploaded to Moodle.', 'Time Limit: Each presentation should not exceed 15 minutes so that a sufficient amount of time is left for discussion.', 'It’s great if you can make a presentation outline to your classmates. Yet, it’s optional.', '', 'Assessment', 'The tutorial will constitute 30% of your total grade.', 'Your tutorial mark depends on three parts: 10% on group presentation, 10% on discussion and 10% on Debate.', 'As for the presentation, tutor will evaluate students’ performance on these perspectives:', 'Do the presenters understand the article properly and thoroughly?', 'Can they re-construct the arguments hidden and express them with their own words precisely?', 'Can they have a logical, critical reflection on the article?', 'Can they raise some controversial but important questions to kick off the discussion?', 'As for the discussion, tutor will assess students’ performance by following criteria:', 'Do they read the articles carefully?', 'Do they take the initiative to express their opinions?', 'Do they try to respond to questions raised by the presenters and have constructive interaction with fellow classmates?', 'Can they articulate their ideas clearly and fluently?', 'Regarding the debate, ', 'Can they provide valid and persuasive arguments to support their stance?', 'Can they refute opponents’ arguments with strong reasons/evidence?', 'Those who come late more than 15 minutes may risk a mark penalty.']
